{"title":"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91cdfa0a53ec9e9961bd0da07045aae026cf5ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,ABC\\,$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> be a triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810b201aa38dbe6a071fc4f500679d0cb9efc275.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,P\\,$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> an interior point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91cdfa0a53ec9e9961bd0da07045aae026cf5ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,ABC\\,$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />. Show that at least one of the angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/2565792b831e2b2793fa982d1021d9301ea06164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,\\angle PAB,\\;\\angle PBC,\\;\\angle PCA\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" /> is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86698178adeaf379c883ce9933633b182caa6315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{\\circ }$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d3645fa769fd8028b5fb6939c519333027340042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d6039925f740fb67c3bf8082b870c16f7ed43337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050b83eb50fce921acbf44f1e6acce3e8a5a7578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238db449db9d3160bfe7052f25e799db23f8dfe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, respectively.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630692aa7ea1d423f8a9664a152e914f94a54c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae01c404d38ea175a79da48008968da6e0820bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/06851db13d6a73445b570930f463a24b4ff13940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64cd0f9104ed8209114f939ba5fe63a529a7e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/cee515f6e4022e0c81fa3d17264b61b141acd1bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7adaf75e3f57ca3464f714538905c2859fa6beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, respcetively.\n</p><p>Using law of sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/0620dbe2d9a3ac8f065e7c656f3a4aad850641b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362478ae29dde45d768148b85c71d08014dd6b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left| PA \\right|}{sin(A_{2}-\\alpha_{2})}=\\frac{\\left| PB \\right|}{sin(\\alpha_{1})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"195\" height=\"45\" />, therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d2064d70d0265e275af492910d55e1644a25963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left| PA \\right|}{\\left| PB \\right|}=\\frac{sin(A_{2}-\\alpha_{2})}{sin(\\alpha_{1})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Using law of sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd974a7eb4b6f9a61239b509d517ec70b3f8026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f66072f51f7a9c836209a9019762af56cb619d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left| PB \\right|}{sin(A_{3}-\\alpha_{3})}=\\frac{\\left| PC \\right|}{sin(\\alpha_{2})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"195\" height=\"45\" />, therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/3/a03c8309b1ca9d1be943efd1d9e8644ae42c424c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left| PB \\right|}{\\left| PC \\right|}=\\frac{sin(A_{3}-\\alpha_{3})}{sin(\\alpha_{2})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Using law of sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b2a657bb32248017252c6638a3eaf502e886193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb4cd56182ef11823f028e389ac02c545379482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left| PC \\right|}{sin(A_{1}-\\alpha_{1})}=\\frac{\\left| PA \\right|}{sin(\\alpha_{3})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"195\" height=\"45\" />, therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94e9906c93a7b578a36ad6c13eb0843ae122284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left| PC \\right|}{\\left| PA \\right|}=\\frac{sin(A_{1}-\\alpha_{1})}{sin(\\alpha_{3})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Multiply all three equations we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e4c5fc1634c04cbb432d577c2f04ada8560d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left| PA \\right|}{\\left| PB \\right|}\\frac{\\left| PB \\right|}{\\left| PC \\right|}\\frac{\\left| PC \\right|}{\\left| PA \\right|}=\\frac{sin(A_{2}-\\alpha_{2})}{sin(\\alpha_{1})}\\frac{sin(A_{3}-\\alpha_{3})}{sin(\\alpha_{2})}\\frac{sin(A_{1}-\\alpha_{1})}{sin(\\alpha_{3})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"473\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe285f57bcc80db444493951d3a2f41d228d26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=\\frac{sin(A_{2}-\\alpha_{2})}{sin(\\alpha_{1})}\\frac{sin(A_{3}-\\alpha_{3})}{sin(\\alpha_{2})}\\frac{sin(A_{1}-\\alpha_{1})}{sin(\\alpha_{3})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"354\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917dd7c90ff27f62158122964edb75ce3ba8903b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"163\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Using AM-GM we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b36c7fd4a1a44fba9bcd94eb8d191490d522500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}\\ge \\sqrt[3]{\\prod_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -26px\" width=\"321\" height=\"66\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a060b19ba588e3be09b360a669032b95db0f8c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"182\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d8344142490ff7526cf601d89b4248b64358fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}\\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"166\" height=\"55\" />.  [Inequality 1]\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5dafea4b73e11c0dfdcc67066b12e0d20bbfd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i})cos(\\alpha_{i})-cos(A_{i})sin(\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}\\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"321\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada9147718327063e68c329a3b3384c4b03c8181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\left[ sin(A_{i})cot(\\alpha_{i})-cos(A_{i})\\right]\\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"268\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Note that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77ff9a1e3b29d70fba5c5c588f9a65d837a2393d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;\\alpha_{i}&lt;180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b2d8fb07ded6287e0cf61fa9415f4a05121912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cot(\\alpha_{i})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> decreases with increasing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c80f9c86b2cec4542f88276ae27938ef614425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b24599915694a978e8e1b92ef6b68e3afe1859.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df9ce1e389cc08716e969be47222f316c64e8f8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[ sin(A_{i})cot(\\alpha_{i})-cos(A_{i})\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"20\" /> decreases with increasing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c80f9c86b2cec4542f88276ae27938ef614425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b24599915694a978e8e1b92ef6b68e3afe1859.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p><p>From trigonometric identity:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682d9fd218e88c03c047fdac4aa33218f7239c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(x)+sin(y)=2sin\\left( \\frac{x+y}{2} \\right)cos\\left( \\frac{x-y}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"362\" height=\"45\" />,\n</p><p>since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f0608fc88c92e41a55af9ebfb192ea4a01607cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1\\le cos\\left( \\frac{x-y}{2} \\right) \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"183\" height=\"45\" />, then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e30d01b6762153d9018b14676452c62f380be541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(x)+sin(y) \\le 2sin\\left( \\frac{x+y}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"258\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b37eed6066318c5700c79edff3d3ccde76cdd54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(A_{1}-30^{\\circ})+sin(A_{2}-30^{\\circ}) \\le 2sin\\left( \\frac{A_{1}+A_{2}-60^{\\circ}}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"447\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>and also,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f482d886d300b0719769b377333bb00b16e781db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(A_{3}-30^{\\circ})+sin(30^{\\circ}) \\le 2sin\\left( \\frac{A_{3}}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"312\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Adding these two inequalities we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d02c8c2200f704538fba3dc3edbf9672066f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(30^{\\circ})+\\sum_{i=1}^{3}sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})\\le 2\\left[ sin\\left( \\frac{A_{1}+A_{2}-60^{\\circ}}{2} \\right)+sin\\left( \\frac{A_{3}}{2} \\right) \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"554\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61e0cf52811be3f6123218c9cab9ee9469541d10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}+\\sum_{i=1}^{3}sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})\\le 2\\left[ 2sin\\left( \\frac{A_{1}+A_{2}+A_{3}-60^{\\circ}}{4} \\right) \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"452\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db5c5caa4e27464d507be714cdb6a7034bb71ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}+\\sum_{i=1}^{3}sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})\\le 2\\left[ 2sin\\left( \\frac{180^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}}{4} \\right) \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"379\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d8b219ecaea07b785e7a87f7f9efa2e54eb910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}+\\sum_{i=1}^{3}sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})\\le 4sin\\left( 30^{\\circ} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"275\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707fcf72cb92ce6b58ef8de775c932e7bc2e8576.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})\\le \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"175\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad4f7a94af561b43a17d3731c43fd783815fb372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sum_{i=1}^{3}sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})\\le 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"183\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b80de785307beacfd23f719d26410853348a2fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})}{sin(30^{\\circ})}\\le 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"175\" height=\"55\" />. [Inequality 2]\n</p><p>Combining [Inequality 1] and [Inequality 2] we see the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8ab2f2e8300b6f508568782352b14f3dda186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})}{sin(30^{\\circ})}\\le \\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"297\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>This implies that for at least one of the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed4b89a6aeb4814026a2be01bde8bd7d264b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />,or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the following is true:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd3ec36a893f3c241007c9f628ba5efa765dd39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})}{sin(30^{\\circ})}\\le \\frac{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}{sin(\\alpha_{i})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"239\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42ba2108f7eb7561142ba65058cbc29ce5098627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{sin(\\alpha_{i})}{sin(A_{i}-\\alpha_{i})}\\le \\frac{sin(30^{\\circ})}{sin(A_{i}-30^{\\circ})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"239\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Which means that for at least one of the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed4b89a6aeb4814026a2be01bde8bd7d264b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />,or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the following is true:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/755fb50da1ff821ed1af64874ac2272d0fd93c59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha_{i} \\le 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, at least one of the angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/2565792b831e2b2793fa982d1021d9301ea06164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,\\angle PAB,\\;\\angle PBC,\\;\\angle PCA\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" /> is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86698178adeaf379c883ce9933633b182caa6315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{\\circ }$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz, orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b08a3523cfbd24be2d29b603bb9fd5216aaf5928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC, \\angle BCA, \\angle CAB \\ge 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"18\" />. Without loss of generality, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e6a41e16562417044ed9abd6fb835d613414770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA \\ge 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9fd62dab964e1812bb6bc4d9650de13ce382bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB &gt; 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647a48ede5a95f3519610762249a4cf365c39c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBC &gt; 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Draw a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714ea4af25a9bfb5adc6b7c3a942da3fbf08493b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, P, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is an interior point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is outside the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Draw two lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceaa64434358882b23d29d5d6c420d2d3a6645cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD, CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> near <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> near <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Extends line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is not tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/845b4c70c969952491a8d23d7f97fa3df4ce2c72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangent point, and simply let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd133d82cfd0bfd5ef816a3249c6d4111883a2b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F = B = E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Draw the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9d3474e139c8e1c2f5902c3cb42d7e47fa7e0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and choose a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/1618db21639943833c9bbb0f81fdf8999d33fbc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GOE = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />. There are two possible points, we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> near point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Draw segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e76fe3b21becefd7798a6d7d40976973bbb6cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OG, GE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78f4d59c4fb1451ec270692c56697dbd1246531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is an equilateral&#160;triangle\n</p><p>Draw segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c486ced4506cdf332c14543c1dd111f78058f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP, OC, OB, OF, PB, GC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed5c249175035bd8c53c0de06ffff35cd5c208a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCE = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\angle DCE \\ge \\dfrac{1}{2} \\angle BCA \\ge 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"295\" height=\"38\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b7b6ed594b9458a300e5219e6bc14649e455d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COE = 90^\\circ - \\angle OCE \\le 60^\\circ = \\angle GOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"316\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07ed0c0c50bac75656edfea4d35b1612dadd05c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle POB = 2 \\angle PAB &gt; 60^\\circ, \\angle POF = 2 \\angle PBC &gt; 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"400\" height=\"18\" />, since we have either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d44caab19262419b1352cef3722dfdeadfe1a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle POE \\ge \\angle POB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba4d64f4175f9d3ea06d209299a95bbcb4a4b0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle POE \\ge \\angle POF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f03ec25173bf29782b316c2e16dc12e00db863aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle POE &gt; 60^\\circ = \\angle GOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad378f9f74b7c53e1b72103d48bb1d27141f2076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COE \\le \\angle GOE &lt; \\angle POE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"218\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/212f437944a8ff09f1286dc0add4a8e42f410f72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCE \\le \\angle GCE &lt; \\angle PCE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"218\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91fc87809f5675ae7183ab400c4458eda7811a62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GCE \\ge \\angle OCE \\ge 30^\\circ = \\angle GEC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"268\" height=\"17\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca95cbb434310bd269581f1cbab4d4f5c6c6a00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GC \\le GE = OG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe12afcb09320aa009f470ecde27d076e2920c35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GCO \\ge \\angle GOC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643be2c871873a179828e3cd08a12c9f57190783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PCA = \\angle ACE - \\angle PCE &lt; \\angle ACE - \\angle GCE = \\angle ACO - \\angle GCO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"529\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3d241f18962cd9eac3f4780b8cbd1ce29be31c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACO \\le \\angle DCO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe12afcb09320aa009f470ecde27d076e2920c35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GCO \\ge \\angle GOC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" />, thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473dc055bbcf9fb3da95a53ffa055257a322f49a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PCA &lt; \\angle ACO - \\angle GCO \\le \\angle DCO - \\angle GOC = 90^\\circ - \\angle COE - \\angle GOC = 90^\\circ - \\angle GOE = 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"758\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We have proved that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9fd62dab964e1812bb6bc4d9650de13ce382bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB &gt; 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647a48ede5a95f3519610762249a4cf365c39c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBC &gt; 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />, the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7adaf75e3f57ca3464f714538905c2859fa6beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f26b41ff015c4255ab404834d4f1e16287916f47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB, \\angle PBC, \\angle PCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" /> should less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>~Joseph Tsai, mgtsai@gmail.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO\" title=\"1991 IMO\">1991 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017182833\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 690/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 26002/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   25.660      1 -total\n 45.51%   11.679      1 Template:IMO_box\n 21.33%    5.474      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25388:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017182833 and revision id 274343. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}